<title>NORWAY: Kvaerner in $100 mln U.S. legal battle.</title>
<headline>Kvaerner in $100 mln U.S. legal battle.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norwegian shipbuilding and engineering group Kvaerner ASA said on Friday it was aware of a $100 million legal action in the United States by the Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi against it and a joint-venture partner.</p>
<p>The action relates to a contract to build a waste to energy facility in North America, a statement from Kvaerner said.</p>
<p>&quot;Discussions are taking place between the various parties concerned with a view to resolving the outstanding issues,&quot; the company said.</p>
<p>&quot;Kvaerner considers that the claim is unrealistic and that it is unlikely that the court will be the forum for resolving this commercial dispute.&quot;</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
